1. Introduction
This project is a fully functional parking‑distance sensor built using an Arduino Uno, an HC‑SR04 ultrasonic sensor, and a 4‑digit 7‑segment display. The system continuously measures the distance between the sensor and an approaching object, then displays the value in real time. When the object becomes too close, the display switches from numbers to a clear “STOP” warning. The project demonstrates practical skills in electronics, sensor integration, multiplexed displays, and embedded programming.
Components Used
Arduino Uno R3
HC‑SR04 ultrasonic distance sensor
5461AS 4‑digit common‑cathode 7‑segment display
8 × 220 Ω resistors (one per segment)
Breadboard
Jumper wires
USB cable for programming and power

If an object comes too close, the LCD will tell it to stop and beep.

